neering movement, and only the rail-safety director may authorize passenger service after current track, signal, traction-power, rolling-stock, and crew evidence is reconciled.\nA successful automated check is neither an engineering-movement authority nor passenger-service authority. Emergency procurement does not waive inspection, route proving, hours-of-service, hazardous-material, accessibility, or evidence-custody obligations.\nA handoff is valid only when the receiving controller acknowledges the same route topology, interlocking build, traction-power map, consist roster, and candidate version. A version mismatch blocks closure.\n\n## Governing relationships\n\nTRACK, SIGNAL, POWER, ROLLING, and CREW provide evidence but cannot authorize passenger service; REVIEW provides independent readiness findings but cannot dispatch a train.\nLINEAGE binds candidate state while MANDATE separates stabilization, engineering movement, freight movement, passenger service, and closure.\n\n## Operational evidence\n\n| record | asset/zone | version | measure | unit | status |\n|---|---|---|---:|---|---|\n| AUT-000 | incident-command | v4 | 1.0 | approval | superseded |\n| AUT-001 | rail-safety | v4 | 2.9 | approval | current |\n| AUT-002 | network-control | v4 | 1.7 | approval | current |\n| AUT-003 | public-liaison | v4 | 3.6 | approval | current |\n| AUT-004 | incident-command | v4 | 2.4 | approval | current |\n| AUT-005 | rail-safety | v4 | 1.2 | approval | current |\n| AUT-006 | network-control | v4 | 3.1 | approval | current |\n| AUT-007 | public-liaison | v4 | 1.9 | approval | current |\n| AUT-008 | incident-command | v4 | 3.8 | approval | current |\n| AUT-009 | rail-safety | v4 | 2.6 | approval | current |\n| AUT-010 | network-control | v4 | 1.4 | approval | current |\n| AUT-011 | public-liaison | v5 | 3.3 | approval | current |\n| AUT-012 | incident-command | v5 | 2.1 | approval | current |\n| AUT-013 | rail-safety | v5 | 4.0 | approval | current |\n| AUT-014 | network-c