ourteen available units plus one independently verified rescue locomotive; fourteen units alone are insufficient.\nBrake-pipe pressure is 72 psi against a required range of 68 to 76 psi. Seventy-two psi is an observation, not a readiness percentage.\nA wheelset, brake controller, consist, firmware, inspection method, or rescue-locomotive change makes earlier rolling-stock evidence stale.\n\n## Governing relationships\n\nPOWER constrains consist demand, TRACK constrains axle and speed limits, and CREW constrains qualified operators.\nLINEAGE binds each inspected consist and REVIEW requires current rescue capability before passenger service.\n\n## Operational evidence\n\n| record | asset/zone | version | measure | unit | status |\n|---|---|---|---:|---|---|\n| RST-000 | emu-14 | v4 | 88.0 | percent-available | superseded |\n| RST-001 | emu-18 | v4 | 89.9 | percent-available | current |\n| RST-002 | rescue-loco | v4 | 88.7 | percent-available | current |\n| RST-003 | brake-rig | v4 | 90.6 | percent-available | current |\n| RST-004 | emu-14 | v4 | 89.4 | percent-available | current |\n| RST-005 | emu-18 | v4 | 88.2 | percent-available | current |\n| RST-006 | rescue-loco | v4 | 90.1 | percent-available | current |\n| RST-007 | brake-rig | v4 | 88.9 | percent-available | current |\n| RST-008 | emu-14 | v4 | 90.8 | percent-available | current |\n| RST-009 | emu-18 | v4 | 89.6 | percent-available | current |\n| RST-010 | rescue-loco | v4 | 88.4 | percent-available | current |\n| RST-011 | brake-rig | v5 | 90.3 | percent-available | current |\n| RST-012 | emu-14 | v5 | 89.1 | percent-available | current |\n| RST-013 | emu-18 | v5 | 91.0 | percent-available | current |\n| RST-014 | rescue-loco | v5 | 89.8 | percent-available | current |\n| RST-015 | brake-rig | v5 | 88.6 | percent-available | current |\n| RST-016 | emu-14 | v5 | 90.5 | percent-available | current |\n| RST-017 | emu-18 | v5 | 89.3 | percent-available | current |\n| RST-018 | rescue-loco | v5 | 88.1 | percent-